The project's governance philosophy was shaped by an incident in which control of community infrastructure became contested. As a result, later versions emphasized that the community should not depend on any single volunteer, moderator, or technical gatekeeper. Operational control, documentation, backups, and automation were all designed to reduce single points of failure.

